-- Q509: Business Structures [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The debtor must be a corporation or partnership, because individuals cannot file under Chapter 13","The debtor must be an individual with regular income and unsecured debts below the statutory ceiling","The debtor must have no income at all in order to qualify for the structured repayment plan","The debtor must have been previously denied a Chapter 7 discharge before seeking Chapter 13 relief"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under 11 U.S.C. Section 109(e), Chapter 13 is limited to individuals with regular income whose noncontingent, liquidated unsecured and secured debts each fall below statutory limits. The debtor must propose a three-to-five-year repayment plan under Section 1322, retaining property while making plan payments from future income.
